To find the binomial coefficient, we use the formula $\dbinom{n}{k} = \dfrac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}$, where $n$ is the total number of items and $k$ is the number of items to choose.

In this case, we have $n = 10$ and $k = 5$. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:

\dbinom{10}{5} = \dfrac{10!}{5!(10-5)!}
\dbinom{10}{5} = \dfrac{10!}{5!5!}
\dbinom{10}{5} = \dfrac{3628800}{120 \times 120}
\dbinom{10}{5} = \dfrac{3628800}{14400}

\dbinom{10}{5} = 252

